# Remaining selected-issue official-source checks

When the owner is checking the remaining selected Path-B issues (currently 293 knowledge gaps), agents and subagents **must** use the internet on official sources. Do not wait for a local quote if an official page can be fetched.

## Allowed network work

- Open and fetch `https://www.legislation.gov.uk/` (including `/data.xml` where needed).
- Open and fetch Find Case Law at `https://caselaw.nationalarchives.gov.uk/`.
- Download official XML/HTML into the configured source roots so local catalogue bytes can be compared.
- Use WebSearch, WebFetch, or the browser tools for those hosts.
- Cloud or local subagents doing this check must be allowed network access to those hosts.

## What still is not gold

- Downloaded or searched text is a candidate only.
- Gold still requires an exact local catalogue or accepted v2-repair match: source version, chunk, locator, and SHA-256.
- Commentary, blogs, Wikipedia, and unpaid summaries are not authority spans.
- Do not invent later treatment for case law from a web page. `confirmed_current` / `qualified_current` remain owner later-treatment findings. `qualified_current` still needs limiting-authority IDs.
- AI remains `mechanical_accuracy_verifier_only`. AI is not `legal_reviewer` and cannot seal overlay, ACTIVE, or O-04.

## Clean room

Do not import the old project. The only permitted old-project path is its `New_materials` document directory.
